# ra_converter output derived from customer SoapUI project XMLs.
# The input XML is gitignored (tools/ra_converter/.gitignore), and the
# EMITTED artifacts (tests, CSVs, request-body templates, audit ledger,
# flow diagrams, suite XMLs) leak customer-internal API details --
# endpoint paths, request/response schemas, test-case IDs, hardcoded
# usernames/emails/IDs. Keep them purely local. Framework files under
# src/main/java/com/hi/api/{data,reporting,rest/utilities,tests/BaseApiTest}
# and tools/ra_converter/*.py are committed; suite-scoped outputs below
# are not.
_audit/
_flows/
tools/ra_converter/converter.config.local.json
Suites/
src/main/java/com/hi/api/rest/clients/
src/main/java/com/hi/api/support/
src/main/java/com/hi/api/templates/
src/main/resources/templates/
# The OpenAPI spec the pom feeds to openapi-generator at
# generate-sources. It is a vendor API contract (endpoint paths,
# schemas, examples) and this repo is public, so it stays local:
# drop it in to enable model generation / schema assertions, and it
# will not be committed.
# Contents, NOT the directory itself: git never descends into an excluded
# directory, so `openapi/` followed by a negation would not re-include
# anything. `openapi/*` leaves the directory visible and excludes what is in
# it, which is what lets the README through.
src/main/resources/openapi/*
# The README is the exception, and the reason the folder is tracked at all:
# git stores no empty directories, so ignoring everything made "where does
# the Swagger file go" unanswerable by looking at the tree. No spec travels.
!src/main/resources/openapi/README.md
src/main/resources/test_data_defaults/
src/main/resources/converter_identity.json
src/main/resources/config/
src/test/java/com/hi/api/tests/imported/
# Generated row files for the imported suites. These are NOT just build
# output: they carry customer-internal data -- measured over 1,064 files,
# 3,721 email addresses, 2,571 account/guest/confirmation ids, 685 vendor
# hostnames and 416 internal Jira URLs. This repository is public, so
# tracking them would publish all of it permanently.
#
# Contents, NOT the directory itself, for the reason given above the
# openapi/ block: git never descends into an excluded directory, so
# `csv/` followed by a negation would not re-include anything.
src/test/resources/csv/*
# The one tracked exception: author-written row files. An author test is
# any class without `.tests.imported.` in its FQN, and
# PerMethodCsvDataProvider looks here FIRST for one, so a hand-written
# row file can actually be committed. Nothing generated is written here.
!src/test/resources/csv/manual/
src/test/resources/testng-b2b-*.xml
# Loose top-level request-body templates left over from earlier runs
# (before the suite-scoped `templates/<suite>/` layout).
src/main/resources/templates/hhonorsenroll*.json
src/main/resources/templates/http_request_*.json
src/main/resources/templates/post_activate.json
src/main/resources/templates/tokenrequest.json
src/main/resources/test_data.example.properties

# Converter scratch space and the cross-suite reuse catalog.
#
# These were ignored ONLY by the repository-root .gitignore, which sits
# three levels above this directory. That works today and stops working
# the moment b2b-api-ai is promoted to a repository of its own -- the
# protection would be left behind, silently, and `fluent_catalog.json`
# plus any snapshot directory the converter writes would become
# trackable on a public repo.
#
# A rule belongs next to the thing it protects. The ReadyAPI XMLs already
# follow that: tools/ra_converter/.gitignore carries `input/*`, so their
# protection travels with the directory rather than depending on a file
# somewhere above it.
_rearch_snapshot/
tools/ra_converter/_smoke_snapshot/
tools/ra_converter/_suite_xml_snapshot/
tools/ra_converter/single_input/
tools/ra_converter/fluent_catalog.json

# Converter backups left by a REFRESH of an author-editable file.
# Ignored wherever they land: support/ was already covered, data/ was not,
# so a PlaceholderResolver refresh left an untracked file next to tracked ones.
*.stale.orig
